      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mount Hope Historical County Park was once a booming iron mining and processing site in the Highlands Physiographic Province.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.morrisparks.net/parks_trails/mount-hope-historical-county-park/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The park\u2019s rugged trails let visitors trek through one of the county\u2019s oldest iron mining regions, blending nature and industrial history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.morrisparks.net/parks_trails/mount-hope-historical-county-park/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hope Mining Company built a church for Cornish immigrant miners, closing in 1984 when the congregation fell below twenty families.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.morrisparks.net/parks_trails/mount-hope-historical-county-park/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community was founded in 1769 by German Moravians, making it one of the earliest planned towns in the United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
